<title>HUNGARY: Central Europe's losses push CESI lower.</title>
<headline>Central Europe's losses push CESI lower.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index sank on Wednesday to close at 1,502.30 points, down 11.74 points or 1.12 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said.</p>
<p>The index fell as all the three markets ended lower.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses. -- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 266 2410</p>
</text>
